# DocIQ — AI Document Intelligence System
# Cursor AI Project Rules & Description
# =========================================
# Paste this entire file as .cursorrules in the project root.
# Cursor will use it as persistent context for every suggestion.

## WHAT THIS PROJECT IS

DocIQ is a full-stack AI-powered document intelligence platform.
Users upload PDF, image (PNG/JPG/WEBP), or text (TXT/CSV/MD) files.
The system sends those files to the Anthropic Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-20250514),
extracts structured information (summary, entities, key fields, sentiment, tables),
stores everything in PostgreSQL, and lets users have a follow-up Q&A conversation
with their document via a chat interface.

## TECH STACK — EXACT VERSIONS

Backend:
  - Runtime:     Node.js 18+ (ES Modules — "type": "module" in package.json)
  - Framework:   Express 4.x
  - ORM:         Prisma 5.x with PostgreSQL
  - AI:          @anthropic-ai/sdk (claude-sonnet-4-20250514)
  - File upload: Multer (memoryStorage — no disk writes on backend)
  - File CDN:    Cloudinary v2 SDK + streamifier
  - Auth:        jsonwebtoken (JWT, HS256, 7d expiry) + bcryptjs
  - Security:    helmet, cors, express-rate-limit
  - Errors:      express-async-errors (wraps all async route handlers)
  - Logging:     morgan
  - Config:      dotenv

Frontend:
  - Framework:  React 18 + Vite
  - HTTP:       axios
  - Routing:    react-router-dom v6
  - Dropzone:   react-dropzone
  - Icons:      lucide-react

Database:
  - PostgreSQL (Railway managed in production, local in dev)
  - Prisma migrations (never use db push in production)

Deployment:
  - Backend + DB: Railway (auto-deploy from GitHub main branch)
  - Frontend:     Render (static site, auto-deploy from GitHub main branch)

