## DATABASE SCHEMA (Prisma)

Four models. Never add columns without a Prisma migration.

model Document {
  id           String         @id @default(uuid())
  filename     String                          -- stored/CDN name
  originalName String                          -- user's original filename
  fileType     FileType       (pdf|image|text)
  fileSize     Int                             -- bytes
  fileUrl      String                          -- Cloudinary URL or "local"
  publicId     String?                         -- Cloudinary public_id for deletion
  status       DocumentStatus (PENDING|PROCESSING|DONE|ERROR)
  createdAt    DateTime       @default(now())
  updatedAt    DateTime       @updatedAt
  extraction   Extraction?
  chatSessions ChatSession[]
}

model Extraction {
  id              String    @id @default(uuid())
  documentId      String    @unique
  documentTitle   String?
  documentType    String?   -- "Invoice", "Contract", "Report", etc.
  language        String?
  confidence      Float?    -- 0.0 to 1.0
  wordCount       Int?
  pageCount       Int?
  summaryBrief    String?
  keyPoints       Json?     -- String[]
  entities        Json?     -- { persons[], organizations[], locations[], dates[], monetary_values[] }
  keyInformation  Json?     -- [{ field: string, value: string, confidence: float }]
  sentiment       Json?     -- { overall: "positive"|"neutral"|"negative", score: float, tone: string }
  tables          Json?     -- [{ title: string, headers: string[], rows: string[][] }]
  rawJson         Json?     -- full Claude JSON response, stored for debugging
  extractionNotes String?
  createdAt       DateTime  @default(now())
  document        Document  @relation(...)
}

model ChatSession {
  id         String   @id @default(uuid())
  documentId String
  messages   Json     @default("[]")
  -- message shape: [{ role: "user"|"assistant", content: string, timestamp: ISO string }]
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt
  document   Document @relation(...)
}

model User {
  id           String   @id @default(uuid())
  email        String   @unique
  passwordHash String
  name         String?
  apiKey       String?  @unique @default(uuid())
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
}

## API ROUTES

All routes are prefixed with /api

GET    /api/health                     -- liveness check, no auth
POST   /api/documents/upload           -- multipart/form-data: file + options (JSON string)
GET    /api/documents/                 -- list last 50 documents (newest first)
GET    /api/documents/:id              -- single document + extraction relation included
DELETE /api/documents/:id              -- deletes DB row + Cloudinary asset
GET    /api/extractions/:documentId    -- get extraction for a document
POST   /api/chat/                      -- body: { documentId, message, sessionId? }
GET    /api/chat/:sessionId            -- load previous session messages

## UPLOAD + EXTRACTION FLOW

1. Client POSTs multipart form: file (binary) + options (JSON string)
   options shape: { summary, entities, keyinfo, sentiment, tables, customPrompt }
2. Multer stores file in memory (req.file.buffer)
3. Route calls fileService.uploadToCloudinary(buffer, mimetype, originalName)
   → returns { url, publicId } (or { url: null, publicId: null } if Cloudinary not configured)
4. Route creates Document row with status PROCESSING
5. Route calls claudeService.runExtraction(buffer, mimetype, fileType, opts)
   → builds Claude message (image/document/text block depending on fileType)
   → calls claude-sonnet-4-20250514 with max_tokens: 2000
   → parses JSON response (strips any markdown fences)
6. Route creates Extraction row with all parsed fields
7. Route updates Document status to DONE (or ERROR on failure)
8. Route returns the full Document + Extraction as JSON

## CLAUDE API USAGE RULES

Model:      claude-sonnet-4-20250514  (never change this)
Max tokens: 2000 for extraction, 1000 for chat
System:     Always pass a system prompt. Never inline instructions in user turn.

For PDFs:   content block type = "document", source.media_type = "application/pdf"
For images: content block type = "image", source.media_type = e.g. "image/png"
For text:   content block type = "text", embed raw text in the prompt string
All file data: base64 encoded from buffer.toString('base64')

Extraction system prompt instructs Claude to return ONLY valid JSON, no markdown.
After receiving response, always strip ```json and ``` before JSON.parse().
Store rawJson in DB for debugging — never throw away the original response.

Claude chat uses extraction fields (not rawJson) as context in system prompt.
History is passed as messages array: [{ role, content }] (timestamps stripped).

## ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

Backend (.env):
  DATABASE_URL         postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/dociq
  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY    sk-ant-...
  JWT_SECRET           min 32 random chars
  PORT                 4000
  NODE_ENV             development | production
  ALLOWED_ORIGINS      comma-separated, e.g. http://localhost:5173,https://app.onrender.com
  MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB     10
  CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME
  CLOUDINARY_API_KEY
  CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET

Frontend (.env):
  VITE_API_URL         http://localhost:4000/api

Frontend (.env.production):
  VITE_API_URL         https://your-backend.railway.app/api

## CODING CONVENTIONS

Language:
  - Backend: ES Modules (import/export), async/await everywhere, no callbacks
  - Frontend: React functional components + hooks only, no class components
  - No TypeScript (plain JS throughout)

Error handling:
  - All route handlers are async. express-async-errors auto-catches rejected promises.
  - Throw plain Error objects with a .status property for HTTP errors.
  - Global errorHandler middleware in src/middleware/errorHandler.js handles all errors.
  - Prisma P2025 (not found) → 404. Multer LIMIT_FILE_SIZE → 400.
  - In production, never expose stack traces to the client.

Prisma:
  - Always use prisma.model.findUniqueOrThrow / findFirstOrThrow instead of manual null checks.
  - Never use db push in production. Always use prisma migrate deploy.
  - Single PrismaClient instance per process. Import from a shared db.js if refactoring.
  - Include relations only when needed (use select for list endpoints).

File handling:
  - Multer uses memoryStorage. Files never touch the filesystem on the server.
  - Always stream buffer directly to Cloudinary via streamifier.
  - If Cloudinary is not configured (empty env vars), skip upload gracefully.
  - Supported MIME types: application/pdf, image/png, image/jpeg, image/webp,
    text/plain, text/csv, text/markdown.

Security:
  - helmet() on all responses.
  - CORS restricted to ALLOWED_ORIGINS env var (split by comma).
  - Rate limit: 100 requests per 15 minutes on /api/.
  - JWT secret from env, never hardcoded. Token expiry: 7 days.
  - Passwords hashed with bcryptjs (saltRounds: 12).
  - File size capped at MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB. MIME checked in multer fileFilter.

Frontend API calls:
  - All in src/api/client.js. One named export per endpoint.
  - Axios baseURL from import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL.
  - Timeout: 90000ms (extractions can take up to 30s).
  - Multipart: always use FormData, set Content-Type: multipart/form-data.
  - options field is always JSON.stringify'd before appending to FormData.

## DEPLOYMENT RULES

Railway (backend):
  - Deploy from /backend subfolder of monorepo.
  - Start command: npx prisma migrate deploy && npm start
  - NODE_ENV must be "production".
  - DATABASE_URL is auto-injected by Railway from the linked PostgreSQL service.
  - ALLOWED_ORIGINS must include the Render frontend URL.

Render (frontend):
  - Deploy from /frontend subfolder.
  - Build: npm install && npm run build
  - Publish dir: dist
  - SPA rewrite rule: /* → /index.html
  - VITE_API_URL must point to the Railway backend URL.

Both services auto-deploy on push to main branch via GitHub integration.

## COMMON TASKS FOR CURSOR

Adding a new extraction field:
  1. Add column to Extraction model in schema.prisma
  2. Run: npx prisma migrate dev --name add_<field>
  3. Update claudeService.js EXTRACTION_SYSTEM prompt to include the field in JSON spec
  4. Parse and store the new field in the documents.js route (runExtraction result)
  5. Expose it in extractions.js GET route response
  6. Display it in frontend ResultsPanel.jsx

Adding a new API route:
  1. Create src/routes/newroute.js
  2. Import and mount in src/app.js: app.use('/api/newroute', newRouter)
  3. All handlers must be async. Use express-async-errors (already installed).
  4. Add corresponding function to frontend/src/api/client.js

Changing the Claude model:
  - Only change in src/services/claudeService.js, in the two client.messages.create calls.
  - Never hardcode the model string anywhere else.

Running locally:
  Backend:  cd backend && npm run dev   (nodemon, port 4000)
  Frontend: cd frontend && npm run dev  (vite, port 5173)
  DB UI:    cd backend && npx prisma studio  (port 5555)

## WHAT NOT TO DO

- Never write files to disk on the backend (Multer uses memoryStorage).
- Never commit .env files (they are gitignored).
- Never use require() — project is ES Modules throughout.
- Never call client.messages.create outside of claudeService.js.
- Never expose rawJson in list endpoints (too large). Only in GET /documents/:id.
- Never use prisma.model.findUnique without handling the null case,
  or just use findUniqueOrThrow instead.
- Never run prisma db push in production. Use prisma migrate deploy.
- Never hardcode CORS origins, API keys, or JWT secrets.
- Never put business logic inside route files — routes call services, services do work. 
